From 7e911054eb889393ddef72990d367e7c2af00cf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:43:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/25] glm cuda: beside DFlash2 the target MTP layer, its
 caches and buffers stay out; the draft head alone loads

With --drafter, the engine loaded the target MTP layer (1.87 GiB a rank), gave every stream's sequence its
attention cache (580 B a token in fp8) and allocated its window buffers, though DFlash2 only borrows the
4-bit draft head made from the rank's head rows. Three things are now separate:

- speculation on (Engine.drafts): the lane core's draft facts and the shared verify windows;
- the target MTP layer needed (Engine.mtp, w.mtp != null): its prompt absorb, chains, window buffers (bm),
  its cache in each window sequence (State.initHead) and its rows in kept states;
- the draft head (Weights.draft_head), owned by the weights: the MTP chains' logits and DFlash2's block head.

weights.load takes Heads: none (--no-drafts), draft (DFlash2: the head alone), mtp (the layer and the head).
--no-drafts drops the head's cache too. Paged sequences (bf16 KV) keep the head's page part for now.

